  "body": "## What changed\n- `crates/app/src/geometry/import/step_closed.rs` finds the shells the file declares closed (`CLOSED_SHELL`, and the outer shell a `MANIFOLD_SOLID_BREP` names) and judges each one's kept mesh (`judge`).\n- `step_facets.rs` (new): each tessellation pass keeps every face's mesh apart, oriented as truck's `to_polygon` would, and records the facet range each face owns. `step.rs` uses it in place of `to_polygon`.\n- `step_seams.rs` (new): the seams of a closed shell, vertices welded within 1e-6 of the file unit, sorted into three faults:\n  - **Reversed face** (a shared edge used twice in the same direction): fixed, not refused. Each face is flipped to agree with its neighbours (exact shared edges, and T-junction sides that run parallel, vote), and each connected group is turned to enclose a positive volume. Logged as a warning naming the face.\n  - **T-junction** (neighbouring faces split their shared boundary differently): closed when every boundary edge's ends and midpoint lie within 2 chord tolerances of another face's boundary. Logged.\n  - **Gap** (a boundary edge farther than that from every other face): refused. `closed shell #id (N faces) meshes open: K boundary edges lie more than G mm from any other face, most on face #F (i of N), up to W mm; the first from (..) to (..) mm[; face #D got no mesh from the kernel]`.\n- A face the kernel returns no mesh for is still refused by name in any shell. Open shells keep the kernel's winding and are not seam-checked.\n- The decision is in `docs/decisions/1573-closed-shell-watertight.md`, including the Prime-Directive call on the two corpus files (below).\n\n## How tested\n- Unit tests (`step_seams`, synthetic cube meshed face by face): `a_face_wound_against_its_neighbours_is_flipped_not_called_open`, `the_flips_turn_the_shell_outward`, `a_boundary_split_differently_on_each_side_is_closed`, `a_reversed_face_met_only_through_t_junctions_is_still_flipped`, `a_boundary_bowed_within_the_gap_tolerance_is_closed`, `a_real_gap_wider_than_the_tolerance_is_found`, `a_missing_face_leaves_a_gap`, `a_face_never_closes_its_own_boundary`, `copies_of_a_vertex_within_the_weld_still_meet`, `the_importer_closes_seams_within_two_chord_tolerances_only`.\n- `crates/app/tests/import_step_closed_shell.rs`: `a_closed_shell_that_meshes_open_is_refused_by_name` (bent fillet_corner), `a_face_the_kernel_cannot_mesh_is_refused_in_an_open_shell_too`, `the_outer_shell_of_a_solid_is_closed_whatever_its_keyword` (pins the MANIFOLD_SOLID_BREP read), `a_face_wound_against_its_neighbours_imports_flipped_not_refused` (box.step with one face's `same_sense` and bound flipped: imports with the same facet count and the same signed volume as the original), `every_solid_step_fixture_still_imports`.\n- Mutation table and real-file table: see the PR comment for this head.\n- Gate (macOS, merged with upstream/main d5a8c518): app lib 246, import 26, import_step_closed_shell 5, import_step_corner_blend 3, import_step_guard 6, large_models 3 (+1 ignored), mcp_model 5, model_fidelity 9, regression_models 2, step_budget 6, step_chord_units 3, step_fidelity 2, step_nesting 8, camcraft-geometry all green; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-geometry --all-targets --no-deps -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- No committed STEP fixture produces T-junctions; the 2-chord gap is pinned through `judge` on a synthetic mesh, and measured on the two corpus files.\n- Face pairs that still disagree on winding after the flips are only logged (8 on 10208, 1 on 32050, both files refused for a gap anyway).\n- The release-lane heavy models.\n\nChangelog: STEP import refuses, by name, a closed shell whose mesh has a real gap and any face the kernel cannot mesh, and flips a face whose mesh is wound against its neighbours, instead of importing a model with walls missing or inside out.\nEffort: high (no escalation; taken over from SKULL)\n\nfork synced at v0.19.0\n\nFixes #1573\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
